  "notes": [
    "The user channel is order-level only: no per-fill price, size, time or trade id. Fills are derived by differencing cumulative_quantity (derived=true, fill_id null, liquidity unknown).",
    "Derived px = delta(filled_value)/delta(cumulative_quantity). For the first fill this is exactly 60000. For the second, two executions (0.002 @ 59990 + 0.004 @ 59995 = 359.95) were merged into one update, so the VWAP 59991.666... is not representable; importer convention: px = null + warning instead of QT-INPUT-004 (SPEC says inexact decimal strings fail; this is a computed value, not a string).",
    "Derived fee = delta(total_fees) in quote currency (USD here; fee currency is not sent, inferred from product_id quote). 2.399800 - 0.96 = 1.4398.",
    "Derived fill ts_exchange = envelope timestamp (ns, message time) tagged record_time: the true match time is not on this channel.",
    "Order ack uses creation_time (us). The snapshot order E existed before capture: the importer emits restate (not ack) so to_schedule does not treat the snapshot time as an entry; SPEC is silent.",
    "Order D: leaves_quantity drops with no fill -> inferred amend_ack (edit), priority undocumented for Advanced Trade -> null. order_type in the WS example is 'Limit' (enum says LIMIT): accept both.",
    "post_only arrives as the STRING 'true'/'false' on WS (bool in REST)."
  ],
